            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "For Maxwell's equations in Hamiltonian form, we use the central finite difference in space (which is leapfrog discretization) and implicit midpoint rule (which is symplectic) in time, it is easy to show that the Hamiltonian formulations in (5) and (7) for Maxwell's equations reduce to the same discretized system,",
